IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `fraud-nouns`
IMPORT `fraud-dates`
IMPORT `fraud-s15`
IMPORT `fraud-penalty`
IMPORT `fraud-s11`
IMPORT `fraud-s12-s13`

-- Fraud Act 2006: TESTS FOR SECTIONS 11 TO 13.
--
-- Every expected value was decided by reading the section and is written beside the assertion.

§ `Tests for sections 11 to 13`

§§ `Section 11: obtaining services dishonestly`

GIVEN obtains IS A BOOLEAN
      dishonestAct IS A BOOLEAN
      basis IS A BOOLEAN
      payment IS A `Payment for services`
      knowsBasis IS A BOOLEAN
      knowsMight IS A BOOLEAN
      intends IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Obtaining services case`
`a section 11 case of` obtains dishonestAct basis payment knowsBasis knowsMight intends MEANS `Obtaining services case` WITH
    `obtains services for himself or another` IS obtains
    `does so by a dishonest act` IS dishonestAct
    `the services are made available on the basis that payment has been, is being or will be made for or in respect of them` IS basis
    `payment for the services` IS payment
    `when he obtains them, he knows that they are being made available on that basis` IS knowsBasis
    `when he obtains them, he knows that they might be made available on that basis` IS knowsMight
    `he intends that payment will not be made, or will not be made in full` IS intends

-- The base case: all of s 11(1) and (2): no payment, knows the basis, intends not to pay.
#ASSERT `section 11(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 11 case of` TRUE TRUE TRUE `no payment was made` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- s 11(2)(c)(ii): knows only that the services MIGHT be made available on that basis.
#ASSERT `section 11(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 11 case of` TRUE TRUE TRUE `no payment was made` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 11(2)(b): "without payment having been made in full": part payment, intending not to pay the rest.
#ASSERT `section 11(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 11 case of` TRUE TRUE TRUE `payment was made, but not in full` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- s 11(2)(b): payment made in full: no breach of subsection (2).
#ASSERT NOT `section 11(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 11 case of` TRUE TRUE TRUE `payment was made in full` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- s 11(1): not obtained at all.
#ASSERT NOT `section 11(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 11 case of` FALSE TRUE TRUE `no payment was made` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- s 11(1)(a): not by a dishonest act.
#ASSERT NOT `section 11(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 11 case of` TRUE FALSE TRUE `no payment was made` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- s 11(2)(a): the services were not made available on the basis of payment (a free service).
#ASSERT NOT `section 11(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 11 case of` TRUE TRUE FALSE `no payment was made` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- s 11(2)(c): neither (i) nor (ii) known, though the person intends not to pay.
#ASSERT NOT `section 11(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 11 case of` TRUE TRUE TRUE `no payment was made` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- s 11(2)(c), fork F6: knows the services are paid for but does NOT intend to withhold payment.
-- Read "but intends" as qualifying both (i) and (ii): no breach.
#ASSERT NOT `section 11(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 11 case of` TRUE TRUE TRUE `no payment was made` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `section 11(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 11 case of` TRUE TRUE TRUE `no payment was made` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- The three limbs of s 11(2) directly.
#ASSERT `section 11(2)(a): the services are made available on the basis that payment will be made` (`a section 11 case of` TRUE TRUE TRUE `no payment was made` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `section 11(2)(b): the services are obtained without payment, or without payment in full` (`a section 11 case of` TRUE TRUE TRUE `payment was made, but not in full` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `section 11(2)(b): the services are obtained without payment, or without payment in full` (`a section 11 case of` TRUE TRUE TRUE `payment was made in full` TRUE FALSE TRUE)

§§ `Section 12: liability of company officers for offences by company`

GIVEN byCorporate IS A BOOLEAN
      consent IS A BOOLEAN
      connivance IS A BOOLEAN
      capacity IS A `Capacity in a body corporate`
      inManagement IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Officer case`
`a section 12 case of` byCorporate consent connivance capacity inManagement MEANS `Officer case` WITH
    `an offence under this Act is committed by a body corporate` IS byCorporate
    `it is proved that the offence was committed with the person's consent` IS consent
    `it is proved that the offence was committed with the person's connivance` IS connivance
    `the person's capacity` IS capacity
    `the acts and defaults are in connection with his functions of management` IS inManagement

-- s 12(2): a director, with proved consent.
#ASSERT `section 12(2): the person is guilty of the offence as well as the body corporate` (`a section 12 case of` TRUE TRUE FALSE `a director` FALSE)
-- Connivance rather than consent.
#ASSERT `section 12(2): the person is guilty of the offence as well as the body corporate` (`a section 12 case of` TRUE FALSE TRUE `a director` FALSE)
-- Each of the other capacities in s 12(2)(a) and (b).
#ASSERT `section 12(2): the person is guilty of the offence as well as the body corporate` (`a section 12 case of` TRUE TRUE FALSE `a manager` FALSE)
#ASSERT `section 12(2): the person is guilty of the offence as well as the body corporate` (`a section 12 case of` TRUE TRUE FALSE `a secretary` FALSE)
#ASSERT `section 12(2): the person is guilty of the offence as well as the body corporate` (`a section 12 case of` TRUE TRUE FALSE `another similar officer` FALSE)
#ASSERT `section 12(2): the person is guilty of the offence as well as the body corporate` (`a section 12 case of` TRUE TRUE FALSE `a person purporting to act in any such capacity` FALSE)
-- Not an officer of any of those kinds.
#ASSERT NOT `section 12(2): the person is guilty of the offence as well as the body corporate` (`a section 12 case of` TRUE TRUE FALSE `none of these` FALSE)
-- Neither consent nor connivance is proved: the position alone is not enough.
#ASSERT NOT `section 12(2): the person is guilty of the offence as well as the body corporate` (`a section 12 case of` TRUE FALSE FALSE `a director` FALSE)
-- s 12(1): the offence was not committed by a body corporate.
#ASSERT NOT `section 12(2): the person is guilty of the offence as well as the body corporate` (`a section 12 case of` FALSE TRUE TRUE `a director` FALSE)
-- s 12(3): a member of a body corporate managed by its members, in connection with functions of management.
#ASSERT `section 12(2): the person is guilty of the offence as well as the body corporate` (`a section 12 case of` TRUE TRUE FALSE `a member of a body corporate whose affairs are managed by its members` TRUE)
-- s 12(3): the same member, but not in connection with functions of management.
#ASSERT NOT `section 12(2): the person is guilty of the offence as well as the body corporate` (`a section 12 case of` TRUE TRUE FALSE `a member of a body corporate whose affairs are managed by its members` FALSE)

§§ `Section 13: evidence`

-- s 13(3): proceedings relating to property.
#ASSERT `section 13(3): the proceedings are proceedings relating to property` `proceedings for the recovery or administration of any property`
#ASSERT `section 13(3): the proceedings are proceedings relating to property` `proceedings for the execution of a trust`
#ASSERT `section 13(3): the proceedings are proceedings relating to property` `proceedings for an account of any property or dealings with property`
#ASSERT NOT `section 13(3): the proceedings are proceedings relating to property` `other proceedings`
-- s 13(4): related offence.
#ASSERT `section 13(4): the offence is a related offence` `conspiracy to defraud`
#ASSERT `section 13(4): the offence is a related offence` `any other offence involving any form of fraudulent conduct or purpose`
#ASSERT NOT `section 13(4): the offence is a related offence` `an offence under this Act`
#ASSERT NOT `section 13(4): the offence is a related offence` `an offence of none of these kinds`
-- s 13(1)/(2): "an offence under this Act or a related offence".
#ASSERT `section 13(1) and (2): the offence is an offence under this Act or a related offence` `an offence under this Act`
#ASSERT `section 13(1) and (2): the offence is an offence under this Act or a related offence` `conspiracy to defraud`
#ASSERT NOT `section 13(1) and (2): the offence is an offence under this Act or a related offence` `an offence of none of these kinds`

GIVEN proceedings IS A `Kind of proceedings`
      required IS A `What is required of the person`
      who IS A `Who may be incriminated`
      offence IS A `Kind of offence`
GIVETH A `Question or order case`
`a section 13(1) case of` proceedings required who offence MEANS `Question or order case` WITH
    `the proceedings are` IS proceedings
    `what is required of the person` IS required
    `the ground is that doing so may incriminate` IS who
    `of an offence of the kind` IS offence

-- s 13(1)(a): a question put in proceedings for recovery of property; may incriminate the person of an offence under this Act.
#ASSERT `section 13(1): whether the person is excused on the ground of self-incrimination` (`a section 13(1) case of` `proceedings for the recovery or administration of any property` `to answer a question put to him` `the person` `an offence under this Act`) EQUALS `not excused on that ground`
-- s 13(1)(b): an order made.
#ASSERT `section 13(1): whether the person is excused on the ground of self-incrimination` (`a section 13(1) case of` `proceedings for the execution of a trust` `to comply with an order made` `the person` `an offence under this Act`) EQUALS `not excused on that ground`
-- s 13(3)(c): account of property.
#ASSERT `section 13(1): whether the person is excused on the ground of self-incrimination` (`a section 13(1) case of` `proceedings for an account of any property or dealings with property` `to answer a question put to him` `the person` `an offence under this Act`) EQUALS `not excused on that ground`
-- The ground is incrimination of the spouse or civil partner.
#ASSERT `section 13(1): whether the person is excused on the ground of self-incrimination` (`a section 13(1) case of` `proceedings for the recovery or administration of any property` `to answer a question put to him` `the person's spouse or civil partner` `an offence under this Act`) EQUALS `not excused on that ground`
-- A related offence: conspiracy to defraud; any other offence involving fraudulent conduct.
#ASSERT `section 13(1): whether the person is excused on the ground of self-incrimination` (`a section 13(1) case of` `proceedings for the recovery or administration of any property` `to answer a question put to him` `the person` `conspiracy to defraud`) EQUALS `not excused on that ground`
#ASSERT `section 13(1): whether the person is excused on the ground of self-incrimination` (`a section 13(1) case of` `proceedings for the recovery or administration of any property` `to answer a question put to him` `the person` `any other offence involving any form of fraudulent conduct or purpose`) EQUALS `not excused on that ground`
-- Outside the section: proceedings not relating to property; the Act says nothing.
#ASSERT `section 13(1): whether the person is excused on the ground of self-incrimination` (`a section 13(1) case of` `other proceedings` `to answer a question put to him` `the person` `an offence under this Act`) EQUALS `section 13(1) does not apply`
-- Outside the section: nothing is required of the person.
#ASSERT `section 13(1): whether the person is excused on the ground of self-incrimination` (`a section 13(1) case of` `proceedings for the recovery or administration of any property` `neither` `the person` `an offence under this Act`) EQUALS `section 13(1) does not apply`
-- Outside the section: the ground is not incrimination of the person or the spouse or civil partner.
#ASSERT `section 13(1): whether the person is excused on the ground of self-incrimination` (`a section 13(1) case of` `proceedings for the recovery or administration of any property` `to answer a question put to him` `neither of them` `an offence under this Act`) EQUALS `section 13(1) does not apply`
-- Outside the section: an offence of none of those kinds.
#ASSERT `section 13(1): whether the person is excused on the ground of self-incrimination` (`a section 13(1) case of` `proceedings for the recovery or administration of any property` `to answer a question put to him` `the person` `an offence of none of these kinds`) EQUALS `section 13(1) does not apply`

GIVEN madeInAnswering IS A BOOLEAN
      offence IS A `Kind of offence`
      against IS AN `Against whom a statement is to be used`
      marriedAfter IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Statement case`
`a section 13(2) case of` madeInAnswering offence against marriedAfter MEANS `Statement case` WITH
    `made in answering such a question or complying with such an order` IS madeInAnswering
    `the proceedings in which it is to be used are for an offence of the kind` IS offence
    `it is to be used against` IS against
    `they married or became civil partners after the making of the statement or admission` IS marriedAfter

-- s 13(2): not admissible against the person who made it.
#ASSERT `section 13(2): whether the statement or admission is admissible in evidence` (`a section 13(2) case of` TRUE `an offence under this Act` `the person who made it` FALSE) EQUALS `not admissible in evidence`
-- Not admissible against the spouse or civil partner (married before the statement).
#ASSERT `section 13(2): whether the statement or admission is admissible in evidence` (`a section 13(2) case of` TRUE `an offence under this Act` `the spouse or civil partner of the person who made it` FALSE) EQUALS `not admissible in evidence`
-- The exception: they married or became civil partners AFTER the statement was made.
#ASSERT `section 13(2): whether the statement or admission is admissible in evidence` (`a section 13(2) case of` TRUE `an offence under this Act` `the spouse or civil partner of the person who made it` TRUE) EQUALS `section 13(2) does not apply`
-- The exception is about the spouse only: against the person who made it, it is still inadmissible.
#ASSERT `section 13(2): whether the statement or admission is admissible in evidence` (`a section 13(2) case of` TRUE `an offence under this Act` `the person who made it` TRUE) EQUALS `not admissible in evidence`
-- Against anyone else: the Act does not exclude it.
#ASSERT `section 13(2): whether the statement or admission is admissible in evidence` (`a section 13(2) case of` TRUE `an offence under this Act` `anyone else` FALSE) EQUALS `section 13(2) does not apply`
-- A related offence is within the section.
#ASSERT `section 13(2): whether the statement or admission is admissible in evidence` (`a section 13(2) case of` TRUE `conspiracy to defraud` `the person who made it` FALSE) EQUALS `not admissible in evidence`
-- An offence of none of those kinds is outside the section.
#ASSERT `section 13(2): whether the statement or admission is admissible in evidence` (`a section 13(2) case of` TRUE `an offence of none of these kinds` `the person who made it` FALSE) EQUALS `section 13(2) does not apply`
-- Not a statement made in answering such a question or complying with such an order.
#ASSERT `section 13(2): whether the statement or admission is admissible in evidence` (`a section 13(2) case of` FALSE `an offence under this Act` `the person who made it` FALSE) EQUALS `section 13(2) does not apply`
